From: l16-linux
Subject: [PATCH] gstreamer: Apply controls under the object lock

set_property() changes the pending controls under the object lock from the
application thread, while the streaming thread applied and cleared them
under the stream lock only, so controls set meanwhile were lost.
---
diff -ruN a2/src/gstreamer/gstlibcamerasrc.cpp b2/src/gstreamer/gstlibcamerasrc.cpp
--- a/src/gstreamer/gstlibcamerasrc.cpp	2026-09-29 23:29:03.265857649 -0700
+++ b/src/gstreamer/gstlibcamerasrc.cpp	2026-09-29 23:29:03.362657648 -0700
@@ -185,8 +185,15 @@
 	if (!request)
 		return -ENOMEM;
 
-	/* Apply controls */
-	controls_.applyControls(request);
+	/*
+	 * Apply controls. set_property() changes them under the object lock,
+	 * from the application thread: take it too, or a control set while
+	 * they are applied here is lost.
+	 */
+	{
+		GLibLocker locker(GST_OBJECT(src_));
+		controls_.applyControls(request);
+	}
 
 	std::unique_ptr<RequestWrap> wrap =
 		std::make_unique<RequestWrap>(std::move(request));
